From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SystoleOS <systole@example.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] COMP: Add missing <iostream> include to SlicerIGSIOCommon

VTK 9.6 headers no longer include <iostream> transitively, nor provide
the global using-declarations for cout/cerr/clog, so code written
against older VTK fails with "'cerr' is not a member of 'std'" or
"'cerr' was not declared in this scope".  Include <iostream> in every
source file that uses these streams and qualify bare uses with std::.
---
 SlicerIGSIOCommon/vtkSlicerIGSIOLogger.cxx | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/SlicerIGSIOCommon/vtkSlicerIGSIOLogger.cxx b/SlicerIGSIOCommon/vtkSlicerIGSIOLogger.cxx
index 5fa5495..d88791a 100644
--- a/SlicerIGSIOCommon/vtkSlicerIGSIOLogger.cxx
+++ b/SlicerIGSIOCommon/vtkSlicerIGSIOLogger.cxx
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <iostream>
